# View & Page Workflow

This project follows a consistent pattern for implementing views and pages, which helps maintain code organization and predictability.

## View Organization

- Views are organized in [src/views/](mdc:src/views/) by business domain
- Each domain has its own directory structure reflecting the application's functionality
- Common pages like Login, Home, and Error have their own directories

## Page Structure Patterns

Most CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) pages follow this pattern:

1. **Index/List Page**
   - Contains a search form at the top
   - Displays a data table with action buttons
   - Includes functionality for creating, viewing, editing, and deleting records

2. **Form Page/Component**
   - Used for creating and editing data
   - Usually implemented as a dialog or drawer
   - Contains form validation and submission logic

3. **Detail Page/Component**
   - Used for displaying detailed information about a record
   - Often uses the Descriptions component for layout

## Routing

- Routes are defined in [src/router/modules/](mdc:src/router/modules/)
- Each business domain typically has its own route module
- Routes use lazy-loading for better performance

## Common View Patterns

```vue
<!-- Example list page structure -->
<template>
  <ContentWrap>
    <!-- Search Form -->
    <Form :schema="searchSchema" @search="handleSearch" />
    
    <!-- Action Buttons -->
    <div class="mb-10px">
      <XButton @click="handleCreate">新增</XButton>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Data Table -->
    <Table 
      :columns="columns" 
      :data="list" 
      :loading="loading"
      @page-change="handlePageChange"
    />
    
    <!-- Dialog Forms -->
    <Dialog v-model="dialogVisible" :title="dialogTitle">
      <Form :schema="formSchema" @submit="handleSubmit" />
    </Dialog>
  </ContentWrap>
</template>
```

When creating new views, follow these established patterns to maintain consistency throughout the application.
